{"title":"Career Roadmap · Radiation Safety Officer","role":"Radiation Safety Officer","summary":"A Radiation Safety Officer (RSO) is responsible for ensuring that radiation-producing activities are conducted safely, legally, and within prescribed dose and contamination limits.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Nuclear Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Radiation Safety Officer (RSO) is responsible for ensuring that radiation-producing activities are conducted safely, legally, and within prescribed dose and contamination limits."},{"type":"p","text":"The role covers:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation monitoring"},{"text":"Worker and public protection"},{"text":"Radioactive-source control"},{"text":"Radiation surveys"},{"text":"Dosimetry"},{"text":"Shielding assessment"},{"text":"Contamination control"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance"},{"text":"Radiation safety documentation"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"Training and safety procedures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a Nuclear Engineering graduate, the role provides a direct connection between nuclear science, radiation physics, health physics, engineering safety, regulatory compliance and operational risk management."},{"type":"note","label":"Important eligibility note","text":"In India, authorization/designation as a Radiation Safety Officer can depend on the type of radiation facility, source/equipment, qualification, training, experience and approval requirements of the competent regulatory authority. A B.Tech/B.E. Nuclear Engineering degree by itself should not be assumed to automatically qualify someone for every RSO position. Students should verify the current AERB requirements and applicable facility-specific authorization pathway."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","hea