"text":"Mass defect"},{"text":"Nuclear stability"},{"text":"Radioactive decay"},{"text":"Half-life"},{"text":"Decay constants"},{"text":"Activity"},{"text":"Alpha decay"},{"text":"Beta decay"},{"text":"Gamma emission"},{"text":"Isomeric transitions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important relationship:"},{"type":"p","text":"\\[ A=\\lambda N \\]"},{"type":"p","text":"where:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"\\(A\\) = activity"},{"text":"\\(\\lambda\\) = decay constant"},{"text":"\\(N\\) = number of radioactive atoms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also understand:"},{"type":"p","text":"\\[ N(t)=N_0e^{-\\lambda t} \\]"},{"type":"p","text":"and:"},{"type":"p","text":"\\[ T_{1/2}=\\frac{\\ln 2}{\\lambda} \\]"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the interaction of radiation with matter."},{"type":"h","text":"Ionizing Radiation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Alpha particles"},{"text":"Beta particles"},{"text":"Gamma rays"},{"text":"X-rays"},{"text":"Neutrons"},{"text":"Protons"},{"text":"Other relevant charged particles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Interaction Mechanisms"},{"type":"p","text":"For photons:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Photoelectric effect"},{"text":"Compton scattering"},{"text":"Pair production"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For charged particles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ionization"},{"text":"Excitation"},{"text":"Bremsstrahlung"},{"text":"Energy loss mechanisms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For neutrons:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Elastic scattering"},{"text":"Inelastic scattering"},{"text":"Absorption"},{"text":"Capture"},{"text":"Activation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiation Dosimetry"},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes one of the most important technical areas."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Absorbed dose"},{"text":"Equivalent dose"},{"text":"Effective dose"},{"text":"Dose rate"},{"text":"Collective dose"},{"text":"Internal dose"},{"text":"External dose"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important units:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gray"},{"text":"Sievert"},{"text":"Becquerel"},{"text":"Coulomb/kg"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"h","text":"Activity ≠ Dose ≠ Dose rate"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Protection Principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Master the fundamental protection philosophy:"},{"type":"h","text":"Time"},{"type":"p","text":"Minimize exposure duration."},{"type":"h","text":"Distance"},{"type":"p","text":"Increase distance from the radiation source."},{"type":"h","text":"Shielding"},{"type":"p","text":"Use appropriate shielding materials."},{"type":"flow","items":["Radiation Source","Distance","Shielding","Worker"]},{"type":"p","text":"Apply the ALARA principle:"},{"type":"h","text":"As Low As Reasonably Achievable"},{"type":"p","text":"while maintaining appropriate operational, technical and regulatory controls."},{"type":"h","text":"External Radiation Protection"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gamma exposure"},{"text":"X-ray exposure"},{"text":"Neutron exposure"},{"text":"Beta exposure"},{"text":"Dose-rate measurements"},{"text":"Controlled areas"},{"text":"Supervised areas"},{"text":"Access control"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how radiation fields change with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Source strength"},{"text":"Geometry"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Energy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Shielding"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong shielding fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Common Materials"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lead"},{"text":"Concrete"},{"text":"Steel"},{"text":"Water"},{"text":"Polyethylene"},{"text":"Specialized neutron shielding materials"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attenuation"},{"text":"Half-value layer"},{"text":"Tenth-value layer"},{"text":"Linear attenuation coefficient"},{"text":"Mass attenuation coefficient"},{"text":"Build-up"},{"text":"Scattering"},{"text":"Shielding geometry"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Basic photon attenuation:"},{"type":"p","text":"\\[ I=I_0e^{-\\mu x} \\]"},{"type":"p","text":"where:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"\\(I_0\\) = initial intensity"},{"text":"\\(I\\) = transmitted intensity"},{"text":"\\(\\mu\\) = attenuation coefficient"},{"text":"\\(x\\) = shielding thickness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neutron Shielding"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop additional knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hydrogen-rich materials"},{"text":"Moderation"},{"text":"Neutron capture"},{"text":"Gamma production following neutron capture"},{"text":"Borated materials"},{"text":"Concrete shielding"},{"text":"Water shielding"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Neutron protection often requires a combination of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Fast Neutron","Moderation","Thermal Neutron","Absorption","Secondary Radiation Control"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Radiation Detection"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the operating principles and applications of radiation detectors."},{"type":"h","text":"Gas-Filled Detectors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ionization chambers"},{"text":"Proportional counters"},{"text":"Geiger-Müller counters"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scintillation Detectors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NaI(Tl)"},{"text":"CsI"},{"text":"Plastic scintillators"},{"text":"Liquid scintillators"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semiconductor Detectors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Silicon"},{"text":"Germanium"},{"text":"HPGe"},{"text":"CZT and related detectors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Detection efficiency"},{"text":"Energy resolution"},{"text":"Dead time"},{"text":"Counting statistics"},{"text":"Background"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Energy spectrum"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to monitor:"},{"type":"h","text":"Area"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dose rate"},{"text":"Radiation fields"},{"t